ITEM BD — Resolution of Arithmetic Bound Violation & Grid Alignment
---------------------------------------------------------------------
1. Cause of Spurious +993.7 m:
   - In compute_au_distribution.py, feature centroids were extracted from all 16,945 ingested polygons,
     while signed_village_results.json contained 16,943 successfully reduced polygons (2 null polygons omitted).
   - A 2-position list index offset caused feature 14,810 (Kalambe in Satara, lat 17.51°N, elev 1032.6 m)
     to be evaluated against the centroid of a coastal polygon at lat 15.75°N, lon 73.75°E (ERA5 elev 38.9 m),
     producing 1032.6 - 38.9 = +993.7 m.
   - When each polygon is correctly matched to its own geometry via its whitelisted src_file and idx,
     zero bound violations occur: maximum dz_ERA5 is +640.5 m, well below the theoretical ceiling of 865.8 m.
2. Grid & Registration Audits:
   - Distinct 0.25° cells containing at least one village: 210 cells.
   - All 210 cells sit strictly INSIDE the 239-cell comparison set (0 cells outside).
   - Sampling method: Cell-centre nearest-neighbour matching the 239-cell comparison.
   - Longitude convention of ARCO: 0° to 360° (converted to 73.5° to 76.5°E; compare_orography_grids.py:11).
   - Latitude ordering: 17.5°N down to 13.0°N (descending).
   - Registration: Cell-centre registered (coinciding with Earth Engine reduceResolution grid).
3. Record Carrying Erroneous +993.7 m:
   - Village: Kalambe (MH, Satara district, Patan taluka, code 7745).
   - Polygon-mean fine elevation: 1032.6 m.
   - SRTM coarse height in village polygon: 851.8 m (true signed dz_SRTM = +180.8 m).
   - True nearest ERA5 cell: lat 17.50°N, lon 74.00°E (ERA5 elev 839.2 m).
   - True signed dz_ERA5 for Kalambe: 1032.6 - 839.2 = +193.4 m (well within bounds).


ITEM BC — Product Claim on ARCO ERA5 Model Orography
----------------------------------------------------
1. Restated Product Claim:
   Across 16,943 villages, 8.28% (1,403 villages) exceed the ±150 m (~1.0 °C) lapse-rate threshold against ERA5 model orography—4.37% (741 villages) require cooling adjustments up to −4.16 °C (Dattathreyapeeta, KA, +640.5 m) and 3.91% (662 villages) require warming adjustments up to +3.37 °C (Nagave, MH, −519.0 m)—demonstrating that forecast orographic smoothing produces substantial bidirectional temperature errors.
2. Role Separation:
   - ARCO ERA5 Model Orography (geopotential_at_surface / 9.80665) is the correct denominator for forecast terrain bias.
   - Area-averaged SRTM is a terrain-roughness diagnostic (subgrid elevation variance).
   - The ERA5-based material count (1,403 villages, 8.28%) exceeds the subgrid roughness count (984 villages, 5.81%)
     because spectral model smoothing depresses mountain crests (domain min offset −255.1 m, mean −15.6 m),
     adding model truncation bias on top of subgrid terrain variance.
